WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.063 --> 00:01.963
(Production Support: MCST, Korea Creative Content Agency)

3
00:02.033 --> 00:03.533
(All characters, entities, events, and places are fictitious.)

4
00:03.603 --> 00:05.103
(Filmed In A Safe Environment With Child Actors' Guardians)

5
00:07.603 --> 00:09.343
Make it hot, please.

6
00:09.403 --> 00:10.473
Very hot.

7
00:11.473 --> 00:13.273
(Cheering For Tak Mu I, Ju Da Hong, And The Rooftop Romance Staff)

8
00:24.523 --> 00:25.523
(Way to go, Tak Mu I!)

9
00:54.383 --> 00:57.153
Blisters are unavoidable.

10
00:57.223 --> 01:00.853
For 3 or 4 days, you may feel sharp pain, burning,

11
01:00.923 --> 01:03.763
or some soreness.

12
01:03.823 --> 01:05.663
If it hurts too much, do not endure it...

13
01:05.733 --> 01:08.463
and take the painkillers I prescribe.

14
01:08.533 --> 01:10.663
Doctor, will it leave a scar?

15
01:10.733 --> 01:12.273
It should not leave a scar,

16
01:12.333 --> 01:15.203
but there might be some mild discoloration.

17
01:15.273 --> 01:17.243
Since you seem very shocked,

18
01:17.303 --> 01:20.343
we will give you a sedative before you are discharged.

19
01:20.413 --> 01:22.313
- Thank you. - You are welcome.

20
01:28.753 --> 01:31.753
You went through all this at the set because of me...

21
01:31.823 --> 01:35.293
Hey, I am really fine. She said it will not even scar.

22
01:36.523 --> 01:38.063
But...

23
01:38.123 --> 01:40.633
Who on earth is that woman?

24
01:40.693 --> 01:44.063
Oh, she is a minor actress with barely 1 or 2 lines.

25
01:44.133 --> 01:45.803
She would show up to the set even when she had no scenes,

26
01:45.873 --> 01:49.773
so I did think it was a bit strange. Looking back, she...

27
01:49.843 --> 01:51.173
She was trying to see actor Tak...

28
01:52.543 --> 01:53.543
I am sorry.

29
01:55.443 --> 01:59.613
But why on earth was it me?

30
01:59.683 --> 02:01.613
I do not know that either.

31
02:03.323 --> 02:05.223
I told you I will tell you everything...

32
02:05.223 --> 02:06.393
once you bring Tak Mu I here.

33
02:06.453 --> 02:09.923
What do you mean, everything?

34
02:09.993 --> 02:12.933
Just tell me why you threw the coffee, lady.

35
02:12.993 --> 02:15.093
I am not a lady. I am Song Yun Oh.

36
02:18.503 --> 02:23.303
Right, okay. Song Yun Oh, why did you do it?

37
02:23.373 --> 02:25.973
- Please call my Mu I. - Your Mu I?

38
02:26.043 --> 02:29.883
Excuse me. You are here on assault charges.

39
02:29.943 --> 02:33.383
Why would someone like him come all the way here for you?

40
02:33.453 --> 02:35.723
He is not coming. He will not come.

41
02:37.523 --> 02:39.593
- I mean... - Detective, Detective.

42
02:39.653 --> 02:40.723
- What? - Tak Mu I.

43
02:40.793 --> 02:41.793
What?

44
02:58.843 --> 02:59.843
Why did you do it?

45
03:01.113 --> 03:03.843
I grew up hearing I was pretty...

46
03:03.913 --> 03:06.583
and that I should become a celebrity.

47
03:06.653 --> 03:08.413
So I thought I was a flower...

48
03:09.923 --> 03:10.953
I really did.

49
03:12.653 --> 03:14.453
A flower that would...

50
03:14.523 --> 03:15.723
bloom fully one day.

51
03:18.193 --> 03:20.763
Hello, I am rookie actress Song Yun Oh.

52
03:20.833 --> 03:21.993
I look forward to working with you.

53
03:25.603 --> 03:27.833
Hello, I am rookie actress Song Yun Oh.

54
03:27.903 --> 03:28.903
I look forward to...

55
03:30.603 --> 03:32.573
Hello, hello.

56
03:34.043 --> 03:36.243
But when I actually went to a filming set,

57
03:37.913 --> 03:39.983
I realized I was not a flower, but just a weed.

58
03:41.183 --> 03:42.523
A nameless weed.

59
03:47.323 --> 03:49.663
Oh, oh, I am sorry.

60
03:49.723 --> 03:52.563
You should be apologizing to her.

61
03:52.633 --> 03:54.163
Yes, I'm sorry.

62
03:58.703 --> 04:00.303
Are you okay?

63
04:00.373 --> 04:01.373
Yes.

64
04:02.603 --> 04:04.143
What?

65
04:04.203 --> 04:05.773
Your shoes are a very bright and pretty color.

66
04:13.483 --> 04:16.323
How could you say that and then forget about me?

67
04:16.383 --> 04:19.623
And why did you not eat the food I gave you?

68
04:19.693 --> 04:22.363
You said you were hungry all day and that it is just how our job is.

69
04:24.863 --> 04:27.393
The waiting time is long.

70
04:27.463 --> 04:29.163
I'm hungry.

71
04:29.233 --> 04:31.163
We're always hungry in our line of work.

72
04:34.333 --> 04:36.443
You're not eating, are you?

73
04:36.503 --> 04:39.473
You keep losing weight, right?

74
04:42.113 --> 04:43.543
Why?

75
04:43.613 --> 04:45.183
Did that convenience store girl tell you not to eat it?

76
04:47.113 --> 04:49.083
Did you forget about me because of her?

77
04:51.253 --> 04:52.253
Can you ring me up?

78
04:55.423 --> 04:57.063
That'll be six dollars.

79
04:57.123 --> 04:58.123
Take care.

80
04:59.963 --> 05:03.633
The delivery truck is coming again around four o'clock.

81
05:03.703 --> 05:06.433
You can buy a salad box if you come then.

82
05:09.403 --> 05:10.403
Hello.

83
05:15.743 --> 05:18.413
Why were you only looking at her? Why on earth?

84
05:21.713 --> 05:23.453
What more do I have to do...

85
05:24.483 --> 05:27.353
for you to notice my feelings?

86
05:27.423 --> 05:28.553
Mu I.

87
05:30.463 --> 05:31.993
I love you.

88
05:36.933 --> 05:39.303
Are you sure it's completely safe?

89
05:39.373 --> 05:41.633
What could possibly go wrong?

90
05:42.803 --> 05:44.643
The handcuffs are on tight.

91
05:44.703 --> 05:46.113
And we're keeping an eye on her like this.

92
05:48.013 --> 05:49.013
Now...

93
05:50.083 --> 05:51.083
I should stop.

94
05:56.553 --> 05:57.853
I should stop being so nice.

95
06:02.463 --> 06:03.493
Because I realized that my kindness...

96
06:05.063 --> 06:07.533
could end up hurting someone else.

97
06:09.463 --> 06:10.463
I have to stop.

98
06:17.943 --> 06:20.243
Detective, you're watching, right?

99
06:23.043 --> 06:24.043
I won't be showing any leniency.

100
06:25.113 --> 06:26.683
Please file for a restraining order as well.

101
06:29.353 --> 06:31.953
What are you talking about? Mu I, I was wrong.

102
06:32.023 --> 06:33.723
I won't do it again, please don't do this.

103
06:33.793 --> 06:34.853
Please don't.

104
06:34.923 --> 06:36.523
- You don't mean it, right? - Let go of me.

105
06:36.593 --> 06:38.193
I was wrong, Mu I. I was wrong.

106
06:38.263 --> 06:39.533
- Mu I. - Get out, get out.

107
06:39.593 --> 06:41.133
Get out, get out.

108
06:41.193 --> 06:43.603
- Let go, seriously. - Let go.

109
06:43.663 --> 06:45.973
Hey. Let go. Mu I.

110
06:55.613 --> 06:56.743
Oh, just stay there.

111
07:00.783 --> 07:02.723
Where's Producer Yeon Ju?

112
07:02.783 --> 07:05.623
- She had to go edit. - I see.

113
07:09.863 --> 07:10.923
How's your burn?

114
07:12.593 --> 07:13.833
It's fine.

115
07:13.893 --> 07:15.803
Because you poured all that water on it,

116
07:15.863 --> 07:17.563
they said it won't even leave a scar.

117
07:17.633 --> 07:20.373
A scar isn't the issue, it hurts right now.

118
07:20.433 --> 07:21.573
It doesn't hurt at all.

119
07:24.273 --> 07:25.273
Right.

120
07:25.343 --> 07:29.483
I heard Yeon Ju on the phone with your manager earlier.

121
07:29.543 --> 07:32.653
The reasons why you had no choice but to mistake me for a stalker.

122
07:34.953 --> 07:36.783
And...

123
07:36.853 --> 07:38.853
I'm late in saying this.

124
07:38.923 --> 07:41.153
At the grandma's restaurant,

125
07:41.223 --> 07:42.563
when that condom guy was there,

126
07:42.623 --> 07:45.833
I knew the masked guy who helped me was you, Tak Mu I,

127
07:45.893 --> 07:49.533
but I was too surprised back then, and given the situation,

128
07:49.603 --> 07:51.163
I couldn't say thank you.

129
07:53.833 --> 07:56.273
We've really been through a lot.

130
07:57.603 --> 07:58.603
We really have.

131
08:00.643 --> 08:01.943
I'm sorry.

132
08:02.013 --> 08:04.143
For making you go through this because of me.

133
08:04.213 --> 08:05.983
It must be really hard.

134
08:07.053 --> 08:08.513
Living as a celebrity.

135
08:15.553 --> 08:16.563
Here.

136
08:17.723 --> 08:18.723
What?

137
08:41.513 --> 08:44.983
I will take this so you feel better, Tak Mu I.

138
08:45.053 --> 08:46.853
I will take it.

139
08:46.923 --> 08:47.923
Thank you.

140
09:00.333 --> 09:01.333
This will sting a little.

141
09:05.473 --> 09:06.473
Thank you.

142
09:10.743 --> 09:13.253
Oh, try putting these on.

143
09:13.313 --> 09:14.353
Oh, okay.

144
09:20.793 --> 09:23.993
- I will help you. - What? No, no...

145
09:42.143 --> 09:44.613
Well, I will take you home.

146
09:44.683 --> 09:47.053
No, it is okay. I can go by myself.

147
09:48.883 --> 09:53.193
Look, I can walk just fine. One, two, one, two.

148
09:59.393 --> 10:02.293
So this is what a celebrity van looks like.

149
10:06.033 --> 10:07.933
(Good Music For A Good Day)

150
10:07.933 --> 10:10.743
Oh? It is Ian Kim. I am a huge fan.

151
10:11.743 --> 10:13.543
Really?

152
10:13.613 --> 10:14.643
Me too.

153
10:14.713 --> 10:17.343
He is the only singer I have ever liked in my entire life.

154
10:18.943 --> 10:20.253
Why did you like Ian Kim?

155
10:21.853 --> 10:23.883
Well, for one...

156
10:23.953 --> 10:26.753
He sings well and has a great voice.

157
10:26.823 --> 10:29.863
But most of all, the lyrics to every song were so good.

158
10:29.923 --> 10:31.863
They really hit home.

159
10:31.923 --> 10:35.463
Have you been to his concert? They are absolutely amazing.

160
10:35.533 --> 10:38.103
Well, I almost went...

161
11:09.363 --> 11:13.303
(Ian Kim the Concert)

162
11:26.253 --> 11:27.513
What are you thinking so hard about?

163
11:29.683 --> 11:32.123
If I had known that was his last concert...

164
11:32.183 --> 11:33.793
I would have gone...

165
11:33.853 --> 11:35.023
Something like that?

166
11:36.223 --> 11:37.563
He did retire quite suddenly.

167
11:38.793 --> 11:41.533
That was Ian Kim's "Let's Walk Slowly."

168
11:41.593 --> 11:43.603
His comeback after seven years is making headlines, right?

169
11:43.663 --> 11:46.733
They say his concert tickets sold out in just ten minutes,

170
11:46.803 --> 11:48.573
so it seems his popularity is still as strong as ever.

171
11:48.633 --> 11:50.903
- I guess he is making a comeback. - Shall we listen to one more song?

172
11:50.973 --> 11:52.603
Sold out again.

173
11:52.673 --> 11:53.813
I guess I will not be able to go again.

174
11:57.743 --> 12:00.613
Excuse me, can I take a look at these books?

175
12:00.683 --> 12:02.353
The books? Oh, yes, of course.

176
12:03.783 --> 12:05.483
(Byeol I and Moon Bear Volume 1)

177
12:09.623 --> 12:12.093
Even if you turn the pages gently, they tear,

178
12:12.163 --> 12:14.433
so I had to tape them over and over.

179
12:14.493 --> 12:15.493
It is a mess, right?

180
12:20.973 --> 12:23.473
Oh, about Volume Three.

181
12:25.303 --> 12:26.813
Back in college,

182
12:26.873 --> 12:30.383
I was working at a building with a lot of publishers,

183
12:30.443 --> 12:33.953
and I picked it up because it was tossed in the recycling area.

184
12:34.013 --> 12:35.753
Oh, I see.

185
12:37.323 --> 12:40.993
I do not know if I should say this right now,

186
12:41.053 --> 12:43.363
but could you please lend it to me just this once?

187
12:43.423 --> 12:45.963
I will read it very carefully and return it.

188
12:46.023 --> 12:48.493
I only need 2 days, no, 1 day.

189
12:48.563 --> 12:49.863
No.

190
12:49.933 --> 12:52.133
When an author does not release something to the world,

191
12:52.203 --> 12:53.803
there must be a reason.

192
12:53.873 --> 12:56.273
- They might be embarrassed. - Embarrassed?

193
12:56.343 --> 12:57.903
No way, that makes no sense.

194
12:57.973 --> 13:00.243
What makes no sense?

195
13:00.313 --> 13:01.313
In that book.

196
13:02.613 --> 13:06.113
To help the Moon Bear adapt well before being released into the wild,

197
13:06.183 --> 13:07.613
they taught it how to hunt,

198
13:07.683 --> 13:10.253
and to keep it from getting used to humans, the zoo staff...

199
13:10.323 --> 13:12.483
deliberately kept their distance.

200
13:12.553 --> 13:16.663
But Byeol I secretly brought it food,

201
13:16.723 --> 13:19.793
petted it more, and even slept next to it, right?

202
13:21.193 --> 13:22.493
She did.

203
13:22.563 --> 13:25.363
Then she got caught by the senior zookeeper.

204
13:25.433 --> 13:26.603
"You are fired."

205
13:27.933 --> 13:29.643
And that is exactly where Volume Two ends.

206
13:29.703 --> 13:32.673
Wow, Writer Kkongkkong is a total master of cliffhangers, right?

207
13:36.643 --> 13:38.143
I was really curious.

208
13:39.583 --> 13:42.313
If Byeol I really got fired.

209
13:43.323 --> 13:46.493
And if Moon Bear is doing well after leaving the zoo.

210
13:49.723 --> 13:51.763
Do you want me to tell you what happened to Byeol I?

211
13:51.823 --> 13:55.063
Oh, no, absolutely not. Do not spoil it for me.

212
13:55.133 --> 13:56.133
I am going to read it in the book.

213
14:02.773 --> 14:05.603
I have a question.

214
14:05.673 --> 14:08.573
You said you read "Byeol I and Moon Bear" before...

215
14:08.643 --> 14:10.713
and found a lot of comfort in it.

216
14:10.783 --> 14:11.813
Oh that.

217
14:12.983 --> 14:13.983
I did.

218
14:20.653 --> 14:23.163
He lost his touch after coming back from the military.

219
14:23.223 --> 14:26.233
Well, I never really liked Tak Mu I's acting...

220
14:26.293 --> 14:29.833
- It feels fake, does it not? - Hey, you know what I mean?

221
14:29.903 --> 14:31.533
Well, whatever happened before is one thing.

222
14:31.603 --> 14:34.173
But if he went to the military, he should do it right.

223
14:34.233 --> 14:36.603
- Think about how much he gets paid. - Exactly.

224
14:36.673 --> 14:38.173
Does he think he is still a child actor?

225
14:40.413 --> 14:44.013
I was so scared back then that I ran away from the camera.

226
14:44.083 --> 14:45.743
- Other than acting... - All right, let us go.

227
14:45.813 --> 14:47.453
- What else can I do... - Okay, go.

228
14:47.513 --> 14:48.613
I wanted to find out.

229
14:53.593 --> 14:54.593
- Hey. - Hello.

230
14:57.023 --> 14:58.363
Your palms.

231
14:58.423 --> 14:59.863
- Excuse me? - Your palms.

232
15:01.633 --> 15:03.103
Take off your gloves.

233
15:06.273 --> 15:07.273
Turn them over.

234
15:09.403 --> 15:11.243
Oh, for goodness sake.

235
15:11.303 --> 15:13.473
What are you going to do with hands like these?

236
15:13.543 --> 15:16.813
These people here have all brushed with death multiple times.

237
15:16.883 --> 15:17.983
One wrong move and you could die,

238
15:18.043 --> 15:20.753
but you could also die because of some amateur like you.

239
15:20.813 --> 15:23.683
It looks like you came here to experience the real world,

240
15:23.753 --> 15:24.883
but you should look somewhere else.

241
15:27.353 --> 15:28.753
But...

242
15:28.823 --> 15:30.693
That world was not easy either.

243
15:30.793 --> 15:32.563
(Sangdong-Ri, Hadong-Ri, Cheonu-Ri)

244
15:32.693 --> 15:34.393
I was about to give up and go back.

245
15:35.533 --> 15:37.433
But in that book,

246
15:37.503 --> 15:41.673
the words Byeol I said to Moon Bear as it left the zoo...

247
15:41.733 --> 15:43.373
felt like they were meant for me.

248
15:45.173 --> 15:47.413
So I mustered up my courage one more time.

249
15:49.213 --> 15:52.113
After spending a year and a half out in the world,

250
15:52.183 --> 15:54.753
rubbing shoulders with people,

251
15:54.813 --> 15:56.323
I started wanting to act again.

252
15:57.723 --> 16:01.353
But why isn't Writer Kkongkkong writing anymore?

253
16:05.823 --> 16:06.833
I am not sure.

254
16:23.243 --> 16:25.913
Oh, I am fine. I can go by myself.

255
16:27.883 --> 16:30.683
You don't have to give me Volume Three,

256
16:30.753 --> 16:31.753
but you should give me what I paid for.

257
16:31.883 --> 16:32.953
(Byeol I and Moon Bear Volume 1)

258
16:33.053 --> 16:34.053
Oh, right.

259
16:37.363 --> 16:38.363
Let us go up together.

260
16:38.423 --> 16:41.693
Oh, no, it is not like I can't walk.

261
16:41.763 --> 16:44.763
Thank you so much for the shoes. I will wear them well.

262
16:46.533 --> 16:48.173
Have a safe trip back.

263
17:25.203 --> 17:26.913
Yes, Yeong Su.

264
17:26.973 --> 17:28.873
Oh, so it just ends with a fine.

265
17:30.543 --> 17:32.413
Well, understood, it cannot be helped.

266
17:34.013 --> 17:36.883
Yes, you should head in soon too.

267
17:36.953 --> 17:37.953
Yes.

268
17:42.893 --> 17:43.893
Excuse me.

269
17:47.993 --> 17:49.193
Yes? What is it?

270
17:50.203 --> 17:51.633
This...

271
17:51.703 --> 17:52.733
I will lend this to you.

272
17:56.703 --> 17:58.103
(Byeol I and Moon Bear Volume 3)

273
17:59.373 --> 18:01.173
What?

274
18:01.243 --> 18:03.013
- Well... - Thank you so much.

275
18:03.083 --> 18:04.783
I will cherish it as I read it.

276
18:06.013 --> 18:08.683
Oh, I am so happy right now that my heart might burst.

277
18:16.393 --> 18:18.563
Thank you so, so much. I will read it carefully.

278
18:33.513 --> 18:35.713
(Byeol I and Moon Bear Volume 3)

279
18:57.303 --> 18:59.103
(Byeol I and Moon Bear Volume 3)

280
19:06.673 --> 19:07.673
Oh, you startled me.

281
19:09.343 --> 19:10.913
What time is it?

282
19:10.983 --> 19:12.783
It's 11 o'clock.

283
19:12.843 --> 19:15.513
Did you sleep? Since what time?

284
19:15.583 --> 19:16.683
I do not know.

285
19:16.753 --> 19:18.683
I think I went to sleep after watching the sun rise.

286
19:20.493 --> 19:23.993
The sun rises around 6 these days. Wow, you slept for 5 whole hours.

287
19:27.393 --> 19:28.463
(Byeol I and Moon Bear Volume 3)

288
19:29.333 --> 19:30.803
Hey.

289
19:30.863 --> 19:33.103
You finally got it. Wow, hey.

290
19:33.163 --> 19:34.173
She refused no matter what you did,

291
19:34.233 --> 19:36.003
but she gave it to you after getting hurt because of you.

292
19:36.073 --> 19:37.173
Well, I do not understand it anyway,

293
19:37.243 --> 19:38.803
but hooray for Gong Yu Il, seriously.

294
19:40.713 --> 19:44.413
Oh, suddenly I feel like thanking Song Yun Oh too.

295
19:44.483 --> 19:46.083
Man, hooray for everyone.

296
19:46.143 --> 19:48.913
Hey, let's go. We have to go to the premiere.

297
19:50.453 --> 19:54.193
Oh my, why are you here only now? Oh my, you are so pretty.

298
19:54.253 --> 19:56.823
Oh, seriously. Gosh.

299
19:56.893 --> 19:58.763
Oh, what are you doing? That is really gross.

300
20:00.063 --> 20:01.963
- Darn it. - I mean...

301
20:02.033 --> 20:03.733
(Let's hit ten million for I Didn't Know Back Then!)

302
20:03.803 --> 20:08.173
(I Didn't Know Back Then)

303
20:09.173 --> 20:10.573
Will you be okay?

304
20:10.643 --> 20:13.143
If it is too hard, we can do it by ourselves.

305
20:13.203 --> 20:15.113
No, it is fine.

306
20:15.173 --> 20:16.413
You do not hear a rolling sound, do you?

307
20:19.743 --> 20:21.653
- Water. - Oh, thank you.

308
20:26.383 --> 20:28.823
Actors, please enter now.

309
20:28.893 --> 20:31.263
Hey, are you okay?

310
20:31.323 --> 20:32.323
What?

311
20:36.133 --> 20:38.533
Yes. I'm okay.

312
20:42.273 --> 20:43.973
(I Didn't Know Back Then)

313
20:44.043 --> 20:46.073
(Now Playing in Theaters)

314
20:46.143 --> 20:47.843
(I Didn't Know Back Then)

315
20:49.643 --> 20:50.743
Director.

316
20:52.243 --> 20:53.383
Congratulations.

317
21:13.603 --> 21:14.903
It's all a matter of mindset.

318
21:15.003 --> 21:16.373
(It's all a matter of mindset.)

319
21:16.503 --> 21:17.503
Do not be scared.

320
21:19.873 --> 21:20.873
Let's go.

321
21:46.933 --> 21:48.533
(I Didn't Know Back Then)

322
21:50.143 --> 21:51.373
(Tak Mu I is the best!)

323
22:03.353 --> 22:04.523
What? No...

324
22:04.583 --> 22:05.583
Michael Jackson?

325
22:07.193 --> 22:08.393
(I Didn't Know Back Then is a huge hit.)

326
22:08.453 --> 22:09.893
(Let's hit ten million for I Didn't Know Back Then!)

327
22:09.953 --> 22:11.563
(I Didn't Know Back Then)

328
22:19.833 --> 22:20.833
Hello.

329
22:25.173 --> 22:26.773
(Gangseong General Hospital)

330
22:29.143 --> 22:30.143
Oh my.

331
22:32.183 --> 22:35.553
- Why are you practicing lines here? - What?

332
22:35.613 --> 22:37.353
People will misunderstand if they hear you.

333
22:37.423 --> 22:41.223
Should we go practice our script at his agency where fans camp out?

334
22:41.293 --> 22:43.123
Or should we go to my house?

335
22:43.193 --> 22:44.763
We cannot do it at a cafe either.

336
22:44.823 --> 22:46.793
There are plenty of empty rooms here anyway.

337
22:46.863 --> 22:49.933
I get why they are here, but what about you?

338
22:49.993 --> 22:51.833
I came to buy them food.

339
22:52.933 --> 22:53.973
Here.

340
22:55.033 --> 22:56.033
Eat up.

341
23:02.773 --> 23:04.413
Oh, wait, you have to put this in too.

342
23:06.983 --> 23:07.983
Eat up.

343
23:09.413 --> 23:12.023
You are acting a little weird today.

344
23:12.083 --> 23:13.453
Why are you acting so out of character?

345
23:15.323 --> 23:17.823
What? Hey, you got some on your clothes.

346
23:17.893 --> 23:20.593
- What? When did this... - Gosh.

347
23:20.663 --> 23:22.733
- I need to use the restroom. - Sure, go ahead.

348
23:24.203 --> 23:25.563
Is it good?

349
23:25.633 --> 23:28.133
You have something to say, don't you?

350
23:28.203 --> 23:29.503
Just spit it out.

351
23:32.973 --> 23:35.643
Well, I have a favor to ask.

352
23:35.713 --> 23:37.443
I heard you are guesting for Ian Kim's band.

353
23:38.483 --> 23:39.713
Yes.

354
23:39.783 --> 23:41.383
I can't find tickets no matter how hard I try.

355
23:43.623 --> 23:45.253
I thought it was something serious.

356
23:45.323 --> 23:47.453
You didn't need to beat around the bush.

357
23:47.523 --> 23:49.293
How many tickets do you need?

358
23:49.353 --> 23:50.693
Two.

359
23:50.763 --> 23:52.423
Hey, don't ever tell Da Hong...

360
23:54.533 --> 23:55.793
What is it?

361
23:55.863 --> 23:57.563
Why did you stop talking as soon as I got here?

362
23:59.063 --> 24:02.073
The conversation just dies without our Da Hong here.

363
24:02.133 --> 24:03.133
Seriously.

364
24:04.473 --> 24:06.203
I think I should get going.

365
24:06.273 --> 24:07.743
It's almost time for practice.

366
24:07.813 --> 24:09.713
Oh, sure, go ahead.

367
24:09.773 --> 24:11.543
I would love to have a date with just the two of us anyway.

368
24:13.243 --> 24:14.953
- I will call you. - Sure, get there safe.

369
24:16.153 --> 24:17.283
Bye.

370
24:27.533 --> 24:29.633
- Da Hong. - Yes?

371
24:29.693 --> 24:31.463
Stop looking at me and eat.

372
24:33.333 --> 24:37.043
Just looking at you makes me full without even eating.

373
24:37.103 --> 24:38.503
It's my ultimate diet, I guess?

374
24:44.243 --> 24:45.243
What?

375
24:46.243 --> 24:49.913
- Hey, Min left his phone. - Oh, you're right.

376
24:49.983 --> 24:52.683
- I will give it to him. Eat. - Okay, go ahead.

377
24:56.093 --> 24:57.563
Hey, Min, your phone.

378
25:10.573 --> 25:12.273
(Rion Ob-Gyn)

379
25:16.313 --> 25:20.283
Oh my. Hey, I was so startled I drooled.

380
25:20.353 --> 25:22.853
I almost broke my front teeth and ruined my shoot.

381
25:22.913 --> 25:24.453
I was startled too.

382
25:24.523 --> 25:26.823
Come on, take better care of your phone.

383
25:26.893 --> 25:29.393
- Thanks, I will get going. - Bye.

384
25:31.623 --> 25:34.863
Gosh, what do you mean, Ju Da Hong?

385
25:34.933 --> 25:37.203
It might not even be true.

386
25:37.263 --> 25:38.803
And besides, even if they are dating,

387
25:38.863 --> 25:40.403
why is your world falling apart?

388
25:41.873 --> 25:43.973
Please, let's live in reality, okay?

389
25:45.003 --> 25:46.203
I am busy, I have to hang up.

390
25:50.983 --> 25:53.043
These two?

391
25:53.113 --> 25:54.653
I doubt it.

392
25:54.753 --> 25:56.553
(Exclusive: Fans Shocked by Setting In Ryu Min and Ju Da Hong’s Photo)

393
25:57.723 --> 25:58.723
What?

394
25:59.423 --> 26:00.423
(Rion Ob-Gyn)

395
26:00.493 --> 26:03.963
But the background is a bit...

396
26:04.023 --> 26:05.593
Wow.

397
26:05.663 --> 26:07.863
That background is absolutely perfect.

398
26:07.933 --> 26:10.733
- How did you do it? - What do you mean, how?

399
26:10.803 --> 26:14.033
There is no other way but to do the legwork.

400
26:15.173 --> 26:17.403
Man, even though you are both Reporter Park,

401
26:17.473 --> 26:19.473
one hits the jackpot,

402
26:19.543 --> 26:21.613
and the other strikes out every day.

403
26:22.773 --> 26:23.783
Gosh.

404
26:33.893 --> 26:36.053
I swear...

405
26:40.963 --> 26:41.963
Do you have something to say to me?

406
26:43.803 --> 26:45.303
That scene...

407
26:45.363 --> 26:47.203
Did you take that picture yourself?

408
26:47.273 --> 26:48.633
It looked like it was taken with a phone.

409
26:48.703 --> 26:50.603
Who does legwork these days?

410
26:50.673 --> 26:52.603
We use our fingers.

411
26:52.673 --> 26:56.843
Hey, in this overflowing flood of information...

412
26:56.913 --> 26:58.583
picking out the big catch is...

413
26:58.643 --> 27:01.553
That is the sensible and trendy vibe of today.

414
27:02.713 --> 27:05.123
- Right? - So...

415
27:05.183 --> 27:07.393
How long are you going to keep getting a free ride?

416
27:07.453 --> 27:09.453
Who says I am getting a free ride?

417
27:09.523 --> 27:11.623
I am not getting a free ride, I am cashing in.

418
27:13.463 --> 27:14.933
Did you fact-check it?

419
27:14.993 --> 27:17.633
I have been following Ryu Min for months.

420
27:17.703 --> 27:19.333
He never had a speck of dirt on him, and suddenly...

421
27:19.403 --> 27:22.933
Fact-checking does not mean they tell the facts,

422
27:23.003 --> 27:26.673
and honestly, whether it is true or not does not matter.

423
27:26.743 --> 27:28.113
As long as it's fun, that is all that counts.

424
27:28.173 --> 27:31.013
- But it is still news. - Come on, man.

425
27:31.083 --> 27:35.083
We live in a world where even news is entertainment these days.

426
27:35.153 --> 27:37.753
Wake up Reporter Park, please.

427
27:38.883 --> 27:41.593
And you should really drink your coffee hot.

428
27:41.653 --> 27:44.563
That way you might actually catch something hot.

429
27:44.623 --> 27:45.623
Right?

430
27:49.693 --> 27:51.303
(Exclusive: Fans Shocked by Setting In Ryu Min and Ju Da Hong’s Photo)

431
27:52.233 --> 27:55.033
They said stay off my phone when I cannot sleep, so I didn't know.

432
27:56.433 --> 27:58.003
Should I do an interview and say I was with them?

433
27:59.173 --> 28:02.073
The reporters called, so I already told them.

434
28:02.143 --> 28:03.143
Good job.

435
28:04.913 --> 28:06.613
Well, Ryu Min is one thing,

436
28:06.683 --> 28:09.013
but I wonder if Da Hong is okay.

437
28:09.083 --> 28:11.923
I was worried about Da Hong too, so I called her,

438
28:11.983 --> 28:13.083
and Da Hong...

439
28:14.053 --> 28:17.763
"If I ever catch the reporter bastards who did this."

440
28:17.823 --> 28:20.093
"I will rip their heads off."

441
28:20.163 --> 28:23.463
"I will tear them limb from limb."

442
28:25.663 --> 28:28.803
She just got all mad by herself like that and hung up.

443
28:28.873 --> 28:30.743
Even if she says things like that,

444
28:30.803 --> 28:32.543
she might be off crying somewhere.

445
28:34.973 --> 28:36.543
Why should I explain myself?

446
28:36.613 --> 28:38.483
I have nothing to explain.

447
28:38.543 --> 28:41.083
- Is it really not true? - This is so annoying.

448
28:41.153 --> 28:44.683
I already told you. Soup, cell phone, and nothing else.

449
28:44.753 --> 28:46.923
Seriously, this article is not even fit for a tabloid.

450
28:46.983 --> 28:49.993
And who makes an article not even fit for a tabloid seem believable?

451
28:50.053 --> 28:51.823
You have gotten old.

452
28:51.893 --> 28:53.723
Who frets over dating rumors these days?

453
28:53.793 --> 28:55.893
Because the other person is Ryu Min.

454
28:55.963 --> 28:58.103
Everyone will obviously think you hit on him first.

455
28:59.803 --> 29:02.073
Anyway, I am leaving. I have a schedule.

456
29:02.133 --> 29:04.073
Do not call me in for something like this again.

457
29:05.173 --> 29:07.173
You really are your mother's daughter.

458
29:07.243 --> 29:08.673
Already going around seducing men.

459
29:10.713 --> 29:14.353
Exactly, I am definitely your daughter.

460
29:14.413 --> 29:15.413
Right, Dad?

461
29:17.583 --> 29:18.583
Unbelievable...

462
29:19.883 --> 29:23.153
It's karma, pure karma.

463
29:25.763 --> 29:27.433
I'm so mad.

464
29:34.203 --> 29:35.233
Da Hong, you are here?

465
29:37.643 --> 29:40.743
I clearly told you. This is my seat.

466
29:43.313 --> 29:45.213
Please come this way.

467
30:00.963 --> 30:03.163
I guess so. Since you managed to take down...

468
30:03.233 --> 30:05.363
Ryu Min, who is famous for his iron wall,

469
30:05.433 --> 30:07.103
wrapping the salon staff...

470
30:07.173 --> 30:09.873
around your finger must be a piece of cake.

471
30:09.933 --> 30:12.003
Is that genetic or what?

472
30:12.073 --> 30:13.543
What did you just say?

473
30:16.313 --> 30:19.383
I said you take after your mom and are good at seducing people.

474
30:20.883 --> 30:21.883
It is a compliment.

475
30:25.623 --> 30:28.293
Hey, you heard that clearly, right?

476
30:29.323 --> 30:31.663
She just threw the first punch by insulting my parents.

477
30:31.723 --> 30:34.263
It is self-defense from here on out, you bitch. Hey, get up.

478
30:34.333 --> 30:35.893
- Let go! - Say that again.

479
30:35.963 --> 30:38.303
- You want me to say it again? - Hey. You crazy?

480
30:38.363 --> 30:39.833
- Please calm down. - Let go of this.

481
30:39.903 --> 30:42.803
- I told you not to do that. - You cannot do this here.

482
30:42.873 --> 30:44.003
Hey.

483
30:44.073 --> 30:45.773
- Are you crazy? - Stay still.

484
30:45.773 --> 30:47.473
- What about my eye? - Hey!

485
30:47.543 --> 30:48.543
You keep doing this.

486
30:49.573 --> 30:51.013
Come here.

487
30:51.083 --> 30:52.913
You are crazy.

488
30:52.983 --> 30:53.983
You must be crazy.

489
30:57.383 --> 30:59.323
Hey, are you not going to let go?

490
30:59.383 --> 31:01.853
- Seriously. - What are you going to do?

491
31:03.153 --> 31:06.793
Hey. What are you two doing?

492
31:08.333 --> 31:10.263
I mean,

493
31:10.333 --> 31:13.563
what if people see you?

494
31:13.633 --> 31:15.573
Hey, you will never be able to beat me.

495
31:15.633 --> 31:18.573
Just admit it and take the roles that I throw away.

496
31:18.643 --> 31:21.973
Why are you bringing that up again? You unlucky witch.

497
31:22.043 --> 31:24.743
- What? Witch? - Hey, stop.

498
31:24.813 --> 31:27.413
Oh, please stop, Ju Da Hong.

499
31:27.483 --> 31:29.713
What are you going to do if the CEO finds out?

500
31:29.783 --> 31:31.283
All the customers are watching right now,

501
31:31.353 --> 31:32.853
and what if they take a picture?

502
31:32.923 --> 31:34.523
Do you not care about your image as an actress...

503
31:34.593 --> 31:39.463
- or your reputation at all? - Reputation? Screw that.

504
31:39.523 --> 31:42.263
- Hey, come here. - Hey, stop.

505
31:42.333 --> 31:43.833
- Oh, man. - Hey!

506
31:43.893 --> 31:46.433
- You have to hold it in. - Stay out of this, Director.

507
31:49.103 --> 31:50.703
(I will be right back from the restroom.)

508
31:53.973 --> 31:54.973
- Hey, by the way, - I am hungry.

509
31:55.043 --> 31:56.613
- Did you guys see that yesterday? - See what?

510
31:56.713 --> 31:58.743
Ryu Min and Ju Da Hong, why were they photographed there?

511
31:58.813 --> 31:59.813
Why did you say that?

512
31:59.883 --> 32:01.413
I am going to become a pig. When will I go on a diet?

513
32:01.483 --> 32:03.583
- This is really confusing. - The diet starts tomorrow.

514
32:03.653 --> 32:05.253
I am sorry.

515
32:05.323 --> 32:08.223
- Would you like a bag? - No, we are going to eat here.

516
32:11.123 --> 32:13.523
- Okay. - This is so good.

517
32:13.593 --> 32:16.863
- Wow, this is really good. Eat. - Hey, you are spilling it.

518
32:16.933 --> 32:19.733
- Why are you holding it like this? - This is driving me crazy.

519
32:21.033 --> 32:23.373
Please.

520
32:23.433 --> 32:25.403
Are we going to Everland today?

521
32:25.473 --> 32:27.643
- Let us go. - Can we not go to an internet cafe?

522
32:27.713 --> 32:29.843
That is even better.

523
32:29.913 --> 32:32.343
- I am full. - Look. Let us clean up quickly.

524
32:32.413 --> 32:34.513
- We ate too much. - Just leave it.

525
32:34.583 --> 32:36.183
- I will clean it up. - Oh, what is going on?

526
32:36.253 --> 32:38.483
Oh, what is going on? You have great sense.

527
32:38.553 --> 32:40.053
- Let us go quickly, hurry. - Goodbye.

528
32:40.123 --> 32:41.253
Goodbye.

529
32:46.423 --> 32:47.833
Excuse me.

530
32:47.893 --> 32:50.933
- Please open the door. Excuse me. - Oh, man.

531
32:51.003 --> 32:53.533
Excuse me, exchange this for me just this once. It is all melted.

532
32:54.603 --> 32:56.373
I cannot do that.

533
32:56.433 --> 32:57.773
Please do it just this once.

534
32:57.843 --> 33:01.173
- I did not even open it. - Even if it is unopened,

535
33:01.243 --> 33:03.173
if it cannot be resold,

536
33:03.243 --> 33:06.583
- I cannot exchange it for you. - Please do it.

537
33:06.643 --> 33:07.853
I am just a student.

538
33:07.913 --> 33:09.813
For a student, 1.5 dollars is a lot of money.

539
33:09.883 --> 33:11.423
Why are you doing this to me?

540
33:11.483 --> 33:13.953
Are you a fan of Tak Mu I or something?

541
33:14.023 --> 33:16.793
What are you talking about? Why bring up Tak Mu I here?

542
33:16.853 --> 33:18.863
Anyway, I can't do it.

543
33:18.923 --> 33:20.193
If so, you should have bought it...

544
33:20.263 --> 33:21.593
after you finished eating your ramyeon.

545
33:21.663 --> 33:24.533
Then you should have told me that beforehand.

546
33:24.603 --> 33:26.433
You are awfully strict for a part-timer.

547
33:27.673 --> 33:28.933
What?

548
33:29.573 --> 33:31.103
Hey, kid.

549
33:31.173 --> 33:32.973
What did you just say?

550
33:33.043 --> 33:35.513
- For a part-timer? - I never said that.

551
33:39.583 --> 33:40.613
- Welcome... - Hello.

552
33:44.583 --> 33:46.153
Do you work here too?

553
33:46.223 --> 33:48.023
Yes.

554
33:48.093 --> 33:49.793
Excuse me,

555
33:49.853 --> 33:51.623
I am in a bit of a hurry,

556
33:51.693 --> 33:52.963
so could you watch the counter for a moment...

557
33:55.463 --> 33:57.163
Do not let her exchange that, no matter what.

558
33:58.763 --> 33:59.763
Well...

559
34:08.743 --> 34:09.743
A close call.

560
34:13.083 --> 34:15.013
Of all times, gosh.

561
34:22.353 --> 34:23.493
I am sorry.

562
34:23.553 --> 34:26.523
I had a very urgent and important phone call.

563
34:34.533 --> 34:35.533
Right.

564
34:37.943 --> 34:39.073
Did she leave?

565
34:40.073 --> 34:42.643
Well, rather than leaving,

566
34:42.713 --> 34:44.283
it is more accurate to say I sent her away.

567
34:45.543 --> 34:46.543
What?

568
34:48.583 --> 34:49.583
Take a new one.

569
34:49.653 --> 34:52.783
Really? As expected, a handsome guy is easy to talk to.

570
34:52.853 --> 34:53.853
But...

571
34:55.593 --> 34:57.663
I saw everything while I was parking earlier.

572
34:59.123 --> 35:01.963
You know e-cigarettes are still cigarettes, right?

573
35:02.033 --> 35:05.233
Your school, the police station, or your home.

574
35:06.403 --> 35:08.373
I wonder where I should call to make it more annoying for you...

575
35:08.433 --> 35:10.403
- so you will quit smoking? - Well,

576
35:10.473 --> 35:12.073
do you have proof?

577
35:14.273 --> 35:16.473
Do you see the security camera out there?

578
35:16.543 --> 35:19.643
And it was probably caught on my dashcam too.

579
35:26.723 --> 35:28.193
Do not ever...

580
35:28.253 --> 35:31.823
bother this part-timer again.

581
35:31.893 --> 35:35.963
And don't call random guys handsome...

582
35:36.033 --> 35:38.433
or smoke after meals or skip class.

583
35:40.803 --> 35:41.873
You understand, right?

584
35:49.813 --> 35:50.913
Thank you.

585
35:53.583 --> 35:56.653
But that day, I bought a new coffee and went back,

586
35:56.713 --> 35:59.423
but you had already left the cooking booth at the kids' cafe.

587
36:01.553 --> 36:03.653
You came back?

588
36:03.723 --> 36:04.923
If I had known,

589
36:04.993 --> 36:06.593
I would have stayed longer before heading to the restaurant.

590
36:07.793 --> 36:10.033
- The restaurant? - Yes.

591
36:13.633 --> 36:17.303
I actually cook. I do not work at that kids' cafe.

592
36:20.473 --> 36:25.113
You really work at a restaurant. I did not even know.

593
36:27.313 --> 36:30.953
But are you going to have that for lunch?

594
36:31.023 --> 36:32.153
Yes, well,

595
36:33.223 --> 36:35.293
since I cook, I do not have time,

596
36:35.353 --> 36:36.493
and I do not have much of an appetite.

597
36:38.663 --> 36:39.663
Wait a moment.

598
36:42.593 --> 36:44.333
Take a coffee too.

599
36:45.503 --> 36:47.733
I will buy this to make up for the one I could not give you.

600
36:47.803 --> 36:48.803
Thank you.

601
36:51.403 --> 36:52.873
Do you want to work together?

602
36:53.973 --> 36:55.913
I heard they are looking for someone to work the floor at the restaurant.

603
36:57.413 --> 37:00.143
- What? - Food is...

604
37:00.213 --> 37:02.053
somewhat like medicine that heals...

605
37:02.113 --> 37:04.323
the heart you said you wanted to create.

606
37:08.153 --> 37:12.693
But this place cannot run without me.

607
37:12.763 --> 37:14.663
I have been here for a long time,

608
37:14.733 --> 37:18.503
so the owner probably will not let me go.

609
37:20.203 --> 37:22.133
- Oh, sorry, am I late? - You are here?

610
37:22.203 --> 37:24.503
Yes. Oh, my.

611
37:27.773 --> 37:29.573
Hey, Yu Il.

612
37:32.643 --> 37:34.253
How should I say this?

613
37:36.883 --> 37:38.883
I don't think I can use a part-timer anymore.

614
37:38.953 --> 37:42.123
- What? - Well, the baby was born,

615
37:42.193 --> 37:44.293
and there are a lot of places to spend money.

616
37:44.363 --> 37:45.463
My brother, who just eats and plays around,

617
37:45.523 --> 37:46.963
I can't stand the sight of him,

618
37:47.023 --> 37:48.063
so instead of using a part-timer here,

619
37:48.133 --> 37:49.663
I'm thinking of working with him.

620
37:50.793 --> 37:52.433
Anyway, I'm sorry.

621
37:52.503 --> 37:54.433
- I'll check the warehouse. Tidy up. - Okay.

622
37:54.503 --> 37:55.503
- Yes. - Okay.

623
38:02.113 --> 38:04.383
- Give me your phone. - What?

624
38:04.443 --> 38:05.443
It will just take a second.

625
38:14.083 --> 38:16.793
This is the restaurant, think about it.

626
38:16.853 --> 38:18.593
And...

627
38:18.663 --> 38:19.823
I'll enjoy the coffee.

628
38:20.923 --> 38:22.763
Okay, goodbye.

629
38:24.293 --> 38:25.503
Darn it.

630
38:27.903 --> 38:29.003
What?

631
38:29.073 --> 38:32.043
He works at a really famous restaurant.

632
39:16.553 --> 39:18.883
I'm sorry for visiting an empty house.

633
39:18.953 --> 39:21.753
Just in case, make sure to apply this.

634
39:21.823 --> 39:22.823
Tak Mu I.

635
39:29.233 --> 39:30.333
He bought a lot.

636
39:46.483 --> 39:48.053
(Min Ye tagged Da Hong in a post.)

637
39:48.053 --> 39:49.113
What's this?

638
39:50.113 --> 39:51.953
(Post)

639
39:52.023 --> 39:53.623
(Da Hong, Who I Met at the Shop)

640
39:53.683 --> 39:55.393
(She is always confident, regardless of who's around.)

641
39:55.453 --> 39:57.053
(I support my people and my work.)

642
39:57.123 --> 39:58.593
(Ju Da Hong looks so calm.)

643
39:58.663 --> 39:59.863
(Min Ye, you're pretty.)

644
39:59.923 --> 40:01.233
(You're much prettier.)

645
40:01.293 --> 40:02.333
(My Goddess)

646
40:02.393 --> 40:03.633
(Our Min Ye is much better than Ju Da Hong.)

647
40:03.693 --> 40:04.733
(Ju Da Hong sucks. Ju Da Hong's bad.)

648
40:04.803 --> 40:06.833
(Ju Da Hong, Stop showing off. What skincare do you use?)

649
40:06.903 --> 40:07.903
(What did you eat today?)

650
40:07.973 --> 40:09.133
(How is she a natural beauty? She's a cyborg.)

651
40:09.203 --> 40:10.333
(Is Min Ye jealous of Da Hong? Be quiet, Da Hong.)

652
40:11.273 --> 40:13.003
She didn't get her hair pulled enough, did she?

653
40:14.973 --> 40:17.213
So this is how she's going to play it?

654
40:17.273 --> 40:18.483
Darn it.

655
40:21.953 --> 40:26.353
Hello, everyone. Hong-a's Crew, have you been well?

656
40:26.423 --> 40:27.793
It has been a while since my last live, right?

657
40:27.853 --> 40:31.393
I know you were frustrated. So I'm going to tell you myself.

658
40:31.463 --> 40:32.663
(Live)

659
40:32.723 --> 40:35.693
I'm not dating Ryu Min.

660
40:35.763 --> 40:36.893
(Live)

661
40:36.963 --> 40:39.403
I'm not dating him.

662
40:39.463 --> 40:41.673
(Live)

663
40:41.733 --> 40:43.333
Maybe our Min Ye is...

664
40:43.403 --> 40:45.543
in such a beautiful relationship herself...

665
40:45.603 --> 40:47.473
that she thought I was too.

666
40:47.543 --> 40:52.383
You know how people in love see everyone else that way too.

667
40:52.443 --> 40:54.013
(Live)

668
40:55.083 --> 40:57.353
This crazy witch.

669
40:57.413 --> 41:00.353
- Darn it. - Eating with the drama team,

670
41:00.423 --> 41:01.923
you probably saw through the articles.

671
41:03.023 --> 41:04.463
How can you believe it?

672
41:04.523 --> 41:06.523
If you can't believe it, go to that soup restaurant...

673
41:06.593 --> 41:08.533
and check the CCTV.

674
41:10.633 --> 41:14.133
Unfortunately, I'm not dating right now,

675
41:14.203 --> 41:17.533
but should I tell a secret only to my beloved Hong-a's Crew?

676
41:17.603 --> 41:20.973
I actually have someone I like.

677
41:22.913 --> 41:23.913
Who is it?

678
41:25.183 --> 41:27.543
Should I tell you this?

679
41:27.613 --> 41:29.353
To give you a little hint,

680
41:30.453 --> 41:33.223
the person I like is...

681
41:35.853 --> 41:38.563
What is this? Hey, Mu I. Hey, Ju Da Hong is causing trouble.

682
41:38.623 --> 41:40.493
Look at this.

683
41:40.563 --> 41:42.363
Oh, man.

684
41:44.503 --> 41:46.163
This is driving me crazy.

685
41:47.563 --> 41:50.303
That's right, my first love.

686
41:50.373 --> 41:53.073
My first love is still ongoing.

687
41:54.173 --> 41:55.313
(Is Ju Da Hong's Crush Tak Mu I?)

688
41:56.373 --> 41:58.183
They're even bringing up Da Hong's old interviews...

689
41:58.243 --> 41:59.813
and making a huge fuss.

690
41:59.883 --> 42:00.913
They're asking if Ryu Min was a cover...

691
42:00.983 --> 42:02.853
and if there's something going on between them.

692
42:02.913 --> 42:05.483
CEO, I think we need to release a statement right away.

693
42:05.553 --> 42:06.983
We already did.

694
42:07.053 --> 42:09.223
We said we can't confirm it because it's her private life.

695
42:09.293 --> 42:12.963
- CEO. - Mu I, look on the bright side.

696
42:13.023 --> 42:15.763
This is what you call viral marketing.

697
42:15.833 --> 42:18.203
Ju Da Hong is a pro, after all.

698
42:18.763 --> 42:19.803
(Kanghan Entertainment)

699
42:19.863 --> 42:21.303
(Rooftop Director)

700
42:22.873 --> 42:24.133
Rooftop Director.

701
42:26.603 --> 42:29.243
Yes, Director.

702
42:29.313 --> 42:31.583
Oh, of course it's great news.

703
42:31.643 --> 42:33.743
I was worried because the movie flopped.

704
42:33.813 --> 42:34.813
Like in that drama with the parachute...

705
42:34.883 --> 42:36.653
and went to North Korea,

706
42:36.713 --> 42:38.323
people will be watching to see if it's true or not,

707
42:38.383 --> 42:41.423
so the ratings will skyrocket.

708
42:41.493 --> 42:44.093
Right, yes.

709
42:44.153 --> 42:45.193
Have a good day.

710
42:47.463 --> 42:49.933
It's sorted. I must be a genius.

711
42:51.603 --> 42:52.633
There.

712
42:59.873 --> 43:01.973
Mu I, take this opportunity to make it work.

713
43:03.113 --> 43:04.173
Even Grandma.

714
43:11.523 --> 43:12.923
(Mu I)

715
43:17.653 --> 43:20.163
Okay, I'm sorry. I said I'm sorry.

716
43:20.223 --> 43:21.633
How was I supposed to know they'd dig up an interview...

717
43:21.693 --> 43:24.633
- from when I was a kid? - Right, you messed up,

718
43:24.703 --> 43:25.863
Yet you're the mad one. Classic Ju Da Hong.

719
43:25.933 --> 43:30.073
Everywhere I go, people ask me if I'll accept your feelings.

720
43:30.133 --> 43:32.243
Well, that's great. I was wondering the same thing.

721
43:32.303 --> 43:33.303
Hey!

722
43:33.373 --> 43:35.673
Why are you yelling? It's true that you're my first love.

723
43:35.743 --> 43:37.473
And it's true that it's still ongoing.

724
43:37.543 --> 43:40.643
Is love a crime? Is my first love a crime?

725
43:40.713 --> 43:43.983
- You scared me. - Crush? So pathetic. Come out.

726
43:44.053 --> 43:45.053
I have an interview to go to.

727
43:45.123 --> 43:46.483
I canceled all your interviews. Come out.

728
43:46.553 --> 43:48.393
- I'm really not going, Dad. - Come out, hurry.

729
43:48.453 --> 43:50.253
- Hey, go inside right now. - Seriously.

730
43:52.123 --> 43:53.423
What are you looking at? Gosh.

731
43:58.033 --> 43:59.033
Gosh.

732
44:20.953 --> 44:22.353
(Yoo Yeon Ju)

733
44:22.423 --> 44:23.523
(Ju Da Hong's Love For Tak Mu I)

734
44:23.593 --> 44:24.923
(Still A One-Way Street?)

735
44:26.663 --> 44:28.933
It was a crush.

736
44:28.993 --> 44:30.163
Not mutual.

737
44:40.143 --> 44:44.673
Yu Il, Mom is sick. I have a high fever.

738
44:44.743 --> 44:46.013
Can you come over later?

739
44:50.053 --> 44:51.683
Okay, I'll go this evening.

740
44:51.753 --> 44:53.323
(Mom)

741
45:05.833 --> 45:08.573
- I almost missed you. - What brings you here?

742
45:10.103 --> 45:11.443
Well...

743
45:11.503 --> 45:12.873
Da Hong's article...

744
45:14.773 --> 45:16.513
I saw it.

745
45:16.573 --> 45:18.443
You saw it?

746
45:18.513 --> 45:20.443
She's been joking around like that since we were kids...

747
45:22.853 --> 45:24.213
So don't misunderstand.

748
45:26.283 --> 45:28.423
It didn't seem like a joke.

749
45:29.453 --> 45:31.323
But what is there for me to misunderstand?

750
45:33.923 --> 45:34.933
Good point.

751
45:36.133 --> 45:37.193
What would you misunderstand...

752
45:40.563 --> 45:42.303
Is that why you came here?

753
45:43.703 --> 45:46.303
No. I came to return your book.

754
45:48.913 --> 45:50.243
But...

755
45:51.713 --> 45:53.543
I did not bring the book.

756
45:54.953 --> 45:56.313
You can take your time returning it.

757
46:01.183 --> 46:04.553
Where are you going? Get in, I will give you a ride.

758
46:04.623 --> 46:06.223
No, I can just take the bus.

759
46:07.963 --> 46:10.163
I am going to miss the bus. I will get going.

760
46:13.063 --> 46:14.303
Thank you for the medicine.

761
46:26.383 --> 46:29.813
(The Kitchen)

762
46:33.783 --> 46:35.793
(The Kitchen)

763
46:39.293 --> 46:40.323
That startled me.

764
46:49.673 --> 46:51.473
Hello.

765
46:51.543 --> 46:53.043
I am here for an interview.

766
46:54.243 --> 46:55.313
You are early.

767
46:55.373 --> 46:57.573
I heard the interviews start at half past.

768
46:57.643 --> 47:01.583
I arrived a little earlier than the time the manager gave me.

769
47:01.653 --> 47:02.853
To show how diligent I am.

770
47:04.483 --> 47:06.953
- Would you like to sit here first? - Yes.

771
47:09.453 --> 47:12.263
By the way, where is everyone else?

772
47:13.793 --> 47:15.493
They all went for a walk because the weather is nice.

773
47:19.963 --> 47:21.033
Excuse me,

774
47:22.233 --> 47:25.003
how long have you been working here?

775
47:26.273 --> 47:29.213
Me? I have been here since it opened.

776
47:32.183 --> 47:34.243
But you are still the lowest rank?

777
47:37.713 --> 47:39.053
If I get hired today,

778
47:39.123 --> 47:40.983
I will make sure you escape the bottom rank.

779
47:45.223 --> 47:46.593
Are you confident?

780
47:46.663 --> 47:48.333
Well...

781
47:48.393 --> 47:52.533
If you give me some interview tips, I think my chances will go way up.

782
48:01.243 --> 48:02.513
Tips, I see.

783
48:04.173 --> 48:05.743
Listen,

784
48:05.813 --> 48:08.313
I heard the owner here is the chef.

785
48:08.383 --> 48:10.113
What kind of person is he?

786
48:10.183 --> 48:12.353
I saw on the internet...

787
48:12.423 --> 48:14.923
that he is extremely strict...

788
48:14.993 --> 48:17.123
and meticulous.

789
48:18.793 --> 48:19.793
For example?

790
48:21.563 --> 48:25.533
I saw it in a video online, and when the soup comes out,

791
48:25.603 --> 48:27.303
they measured it three times,

792
48:27.363 --> 48:29.303
and the soup temperature was exactly the same.

793
48:29.373 --> 48:31.073
Even down to the decimal point.

794
48:32.403 --> 48:33.443
It gave me goosebumps.

795
48:34.943 --> 48:36.843
There was even a comment below it.

796
48:37.913 --> 48:42.713
Asking if the owner here is some kind of weirdo who feels joy...

797
48:42.783 --> 48:44.053
from perfect cooking.

798
48:48.553 --> 48:50.353
That is not actually true, is it?

799
48:51.353 --> 48:54.123
Well, I do not know. I suppose it might be true.

800
48:57.763 --> 49:00.803
Can I ask you one thing?

801
49:00.863 --> 49:03.473
- Yes. - What made you decide...

802
49:03.533 --> 49:05.303
to interview here today?

803
49:05.373 --> 49:07.173
Was the timing just right for a job change?

804
49:09.673 --> 49:13.243
That is part of it, but last time, I heard someone say...

805
49:13.313 --> 49:16.683
that food is like medicine that heals a person's heart.

806
49:16.753 --> 49:19.783
Hearing that made me curious.

807
49:19.853 --> 49:25.123
What kind of food do they sell here, and what kind of people make it.

808
49:25.193 --> 49:27.863
And if the customers really get healed.

809
49:29.133 --> 49:31.933
But you could find that out by coming as a customer.

810
49:32.003 --> 49:35.103
Oh, I would never come here as a customer.

811
49:35.173 --> 49:37.603
- Why not? - You give tiny portions here...

812
49:37.673 --> 49:40.543
and it is ridiculously expensive. But the wait is also long.

813
49:41.773 --> 49:43.213
I will admit that.

814
49:43.273 --> 49:45.413
I am not saying that is a bad thing.

815
49:45.483 --> 49:48.653
I just mean it's a bit out of my budget.

816
49:54.683 --> 49:57.723
Now. Shall we start the interview?

817
49:59.723 --> 50:03.193
- Excuse me? - I am late to introduce myself.

818
50:03.263 --> 50:05.633
I am the owner and chef of The Kitchen,

819
50:05.703 --> 50:06.703
Kang Hee Su.

820
50:14.143 --> 50:15.573
You know,

821
50:15.643 --> 50:20.013
the one who feels joy the more perfect the dish is...

822
50:20.083 --> 50:21.143
That pervert.

823
50:28.953 --> 50:30.693
Well,

824
50:30.753 --> 50:32.863
should I just leave now?

825
50:33.893 --> 50:36.033
Yes, if you want to.

826
50:37.193 --> 50:38.233
I am sorry.

827
50:41.463 --> 50:42.673
Darn it.

828
50:43.433 --> 50:45.143
You can start working next week.

829
50:46.603 --> 50:47.603
What?

830
50:51.913 --> 50:53.913
(The Kitchen)

831
50:57.583 --> 50:58.653
Seriously.

832
51:03.253 --> 51:06.393
But why did I actually get hired?

833
51:09.563 --> 51:10.793
Is he really a pervert?

834
51:15.773 --> 51:17.733
Mom, I am getting on the bus now.

835
51:17.803 --> 51:19.143
(Mom)

836
51:32.023 --> 51:33.053
Two people.

837
51:40.093 --> 51:44.033
CEO Ju had my manager watch me and take my phone away.

838
51:44.093 --> 51:45.363
And if you are wondering who CEO Ju is,

839
51:45.433 --> 51:47.603
he is my dad and the CEO of my agency.

840
51:47.663 --> 51:48.673
But let me start with this.

841
51:48.733 --> 51:51.533
- The reason I was grounded is... - I think I know.

842
51:53.173 --> 51:55.973
Anyway, I barely managed to find my phone and sneak out.

843
51:57.013 --> 52:01.143
I got out, but had no one to call...

844
52:01.213 --> 52:05.113
and was wondering where to go, when I saw you.

845
52:05.183 --> 52:06.723
So I just followed you on.

846
52:08.153 --> 52:10.423
But where are you going? Not home?

847
52:11.053 --> 52:12.923
My mom's house.

848
52:13.963 --> 52:16.663
But did we agree to speak casually?

849
52:20.203 --> 52:23.973
I have an allergy to formal speech. And since we decided to be friends,

850
52:24.033 --> 52:25.743
we should automatically drop the formalities.

851
52:27.503 --> 52:28.643
Sure, sounds good.

852
52:29.713 --> 52:33.083
But where are you going to go when we get off, Da Hong?

853
52:33.143 --> 52:35.783
Me? I am going to follow you.

854
52:43.823 --> 52:46.093
Are you really going to follow me to my house?

855
52:46.163 --> 52:48.793
Yes. I have nowhere to go right now...

856
52:48.863 --> 52:52.803
and no money. I do not know this neighborhood,

857
52:52.863 --> 52:55.233
and you are the only person I know here.

858
52:55.303 --> 52:56.503
Still,

859
52:56.573 --> 53:00.003
who runs away from home so helplessly like this?

860
53:00.073 --> 53:02.613
Like I said, it is an escape, not running away,

861
53:02.673 --> 53:04.113
so it was pretty urgent.

862
53:05.813 --> 53:08.983
Right now, I feel like that plant hanging in your window,

863
53:09.053 --> 53:10.653
just floating around.

864
53:11.713 --> 53:14.453
I want to put my roots down with you just for today.

865
53:14.523 --> 53:15.593
Can I not?

866
53:22.763 --> 53:23.833
Mom.

867
53:24.633 --> 53:25.633
Mom.

868
53:31.003 --> 53:32.073
Where did she go?

869
53:42.413 --> 53:44.053
It looks like a drama set.

870
53:45.153 --> 53:47.083
It is an old house.

871
53:47.153 --> 53:48.223
Is this your room?

872
53:53.293 --> 53:55.093
Why do you have so many books?

873
53:57.033 --> 53:58.233
What?

874
53:58.293 --> 54:00.763
That's what Mu I used to read all the time.

875
54:00.833 --> 54:01.973
You're here, sweetie?

876
54:04.333 --> 54:05.603
Mom.

877
54:05.673 --> 54:08.073
I thought you were sick. Where did you go?

878
54:08.143 --> 54:10.713
The hair salon. I felt a bit better.

879
54:10.773 --> 54:12.813
Oh, we have a guest.

880
54:12.883 --> 54:14.313
You look like Ju Da Hong.

881
54:15.513 --> 54:18.823
Hello. I am that Ju Da Hong.

882
54:18.883 --> 54:19.983
But what should we do?

883
54:31.533 --> 54:33.503
- Let's talk. - Let go of me.

884
54:33.563 --> 54:36.173
- It'll just take a second. - Talk about what?

885
54:36.233 --> 54:39.573
With a father who keeps two families because he likes another woman,

886
54:39.643 --> 54:43.043
should I say it's been a while and smile while we eat together?

887
54:43.113 --> 54:45.543
Should I ask how she's doing...

888
54:45.613 --> 54:46.743
and ask when you'll come visit us again...

889
54:46.813 --> 54:48.143
to make plans?

890
54:50.183 --> 54:52.053
Don't ever do this again.

891
54:52.123 --> 54:53.553
Because next time, I won't see you either, Mom.

892
54:54.583 --> 54:55.593
Yu Il.

893
55:00.723 --> 55:01.723
Yu Il.

894
55:15.003 --> 55:17.173
I thought I was finally going to get a home-cooked meal.

895
55:18.573 --> 55:20.343
Sorry.

896
55:20.413 --> 55:21.413
But...

897
55:21.483 --> 55:24.583
it would have been pretty awkward if we sat there and ate.

898
55:24.653 --> 55:26.223
What are you going to do now?

899
55:26.283 --> 55:29.593
I don't know. I don't want to go back inside,

900
55:29.653 --> 55:32.793
but it feels wrong to go home like this.

901
55:32.863 --> 55:34.423
Come on,

902
55:34.493 --> 55:37.833
who runs away from home without a plan like this?

903
55:37.893 --> 55:41.503
As you saw, it wasn't running away, it was an escape.

904
55:41.563 --> 55:42.803
It was pretty urgent.

905
55:45.173 --> 55:46.173
Man.

906
55:47.903 --> 55:49.313
You have it better.

907
55:50.673 --> 55:53.243
My mom and dad both cheated on each other.

908
55:53.313 --> 55:56.383
And both with actors. The whole country knows.

909
55:56.453 --> 55:58.313
When I had that scandal with Ryu Min,

910
55:58.383 --> 56:00.553
they told me I take after my mom and seduce men.

911
56:01.683 --> 56:03.053
